        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Annual Tin Cup Challenge Kicks Off on March 10</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/82937.webp" alt="Annual Tin Cup Challenge Kicks Off on March 10" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>The Community Foundation of Teton Valley is pleased to announce the launch of the 19th Annual Tin Cup Challenge and the official opening of the application period. A <a href="https://cftetonvalley.org/event/tin-cup-kick-off-meeting/">Kick-Off Meeting</a> will be held on Tuesday, March 10, from 9 to 10 AM at the Community Foundation office, 189 North Main Street, Suite 112, in Driggs.  </p>

<p>The Kick-Off marks the&nbsp;beginning&nbsp;of this year’s Tin Cup cycle and provides participating nonprofits&nbsp;with essential guidance. The first half-hour (9:00&nbsp;-9:30 AM) is required for organizations that have never&nbsp;participated&nbsp;in the Tin Cup Challenge or have not&nbsp;participated&nbsp;in&nbsp;more than two years.&nbsp;Beginning at&nbsp;9:30 AM, the session will&nbsp;include a&nbsp;review&nbsp;of&nbsp;the new application system&nbsp;and offer&nbsp;personalized&nbsp;assistance. New Executive&nbsp;Directors or staff responsible for overseeing Tin Cup participation are&nbsp;strongly encouraged&nbsp;to attend.&nbsp;</p>

<p>This informational meeting&nbsp;will cover&nbsp;the application process, guidelines, and&nbsp;key&nbsp;dates. According to Brian Thysell, Community Foundation Program Manager, <em>“This is a fantastic opportunity for nonprofits to gather essential information and</em><em>&nbsp;</em><em>get</em><em>&nbsp;</em><em>their questions answered before heading into the busy summer months. Preparing early allows organizations to plan strategically and maximize their impact.”</em><em>&nbsp;</em></p>

<p>Serving&nbsp;as&nbsp;both&nbsp;a six-week giving period and a one-day celebration of community generosity, the Tin Cup Challenge has raised $30.8&nbsp;million over the&nbsp;past 18 years for nonprofits across Teton Valley. These funds bolster&nbsp;essential&nbsp;community&nbsp;services,&nbsp;including youth programs, arts and cultural initiatives, environmental stewardship&nbsp;projects, health programs, and other efforts&nbsp;that contribute to a vibrant, thriving valley.&nbsp;</p>

<p>Executive Director&nbsp;Bonnie Self&nbsp;emphasizes the broad&nbsp;impact: <em>“The Tin Cup Challenge inspires those who care about Teton Valley to</em><em>&nbsp;</em><em>take action. Every donation matters and creates a</em><em>&nbsp;</em><em>meaningful</em><em>&nbsp;</em><em>impact for local nonprofits.”</em><em>  </em><em>&nbsp;</em><em></em></p>

<p>By preparing early, nonprofits position themselves to effectively engage donors and maximize both the giving period&nbsp;and Event Day.&nbsp;Organizations&nbsp;planning&nbsp;to&nbsp;attend&nbsp;should <a href="https://cftetonvalley.org/event/2025-tin-cup-kick-off-meeting/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">RSVP</a> through the Foundation’s&nbsp;website&nbsp;or contact Brian Thysell at bthysell@cftetonvalley.org by 5 PM on Friday, March&nbsp;6.  &nbsp;</p>

<p>Please also mark your calendars for the 19th Annual Tin Cup Challenge Event Day on July 18, 2026&nbsp;– always the third Saturday in July.&nbsp;The celebration&nbsp;features a competitive&nbsp;5K, 10K, or Fun Run/Walk,&nbsp;a&nbsp;complimentary breakfast, and&nbsp;engaging&nbsp;nonprofit booths&nbsp;and&nbsp;activities from 9 AM to Noon at the Driggs City Park.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
